WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.801
-Our first guest tonight is
a talented actor you know best

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.004
as Peter Parker from both
the "Spider-Man" movies

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.205
and the "Avengers" franchise.

00:00:06.205 --> 00:00:08.608
He returns in
"Spider-Man: No Way Home,"

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.875
which premieres exclusively

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:11.978
in theaters and IMAX
on December 17th.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:13.178
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:14.481
-That's right, folks.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:17.116
Spider-Man is in fact
Peter Parker.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:19.185
-Are you Spider-Man's
girlfriend?

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:21.354
Are you Spider-Man's girlfriend?

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.523
-Whoa, it's him!
-Uh, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.924
Please don't touch her, sir.
-You're just a kid?

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.693
-You murdered Mysterio?
-Uh...

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.927
-You helped him murder Mysterio?

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.596
-No, I didn't --
-Come on, let's see that face.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.697
-Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.799
-All this time,
people looked up to this boy

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:35.101
and called him a hero.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.535
Well, I'll tell you
what I call him --

00:00:36.535 --> 00:00:38.337
public enemy number one!

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:41.707
-No, no, no! I told you I never
want to do this ever again!

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:43.209
-M.J., I'm so sorry,

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.510
but I can't see anything
with your hand in my --

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.779
-Sorry, I'm sorry!

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:48.180
[ Breathing rapidly ]

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.715
[ Cellphone vibrates ]
-Dude!

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:50.816
-Dude!
-Dude!

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.485
-Dude!
-Dude!

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.953
-Dude!

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.722
-Dude!
-[ Gasps ]

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.089
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.792
-Please welcome back to the show
Tom Holland, everybody!

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:01.527
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:10.636 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:10.636 --> 00:01:19.746 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:22.081
So nice to see you.
-Dude!

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.282
-Dude!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:25.251
I mean, I've been there.
That's how I get mobbed

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.219
when I walk out of the studio.
-It's tough, right?

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.488
-That was like watching a
documentary about my life, yeah.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.559
-Another day in the life.
-Another day in the life.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.026
It's so nice to have you
here in studio.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:36.028
Thanks for making the trip.
-Mate, it's so good to be back.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:37.964
Thank you for having me.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:40.099
-I want to mention that I have
not seen the film

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.734
because I understand, you know,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.270
these Marvel things
are tight-wrapped.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.039
-Yes.
-They sent me -- They said,

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:48.241
"Would you like to watch the
first 40 minutes of the film?"

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.308
-Right.
-I was like,

00:01:49.308 --> 00:01:50.743
"I don't think I could do that.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.979
I think it would just be too
hard to only watch 40 minutes

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:54.781
and then have to wait."

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.184
-It's like a really,
really offensive trailer.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.552
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.653
-You know? It's really,
really unfair, that.

00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:05.058
We've been showing the press
40 minutes of the film.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.993
-Yeah?
-Just to kind of --

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.562
There's some really big stuff in
this film that we want to keep

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:13.198
a secret just because this film
really is the celebration

00:02:13.198 --> 00:02:14.667
of three generations of cinema.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:18.538
So we want to keep as much of it
back as possible.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.907
It has been really interesting
only talking about

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:23.376
40 minutes of a movie, though.
-Right.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.744
-But it's been fun and the press
have been really excited,

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:27.947
and it's been a really good
press tour so far.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.516
-Do you ever feel like
you're in class

00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:32.851
and the teacher's asked you
if you read the whole book

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:34.320
and you're faking it?

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.555
They're like,
"What was your favorite part

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.156
of 'Tale of Two Cities'?"
"The beginning. Oh."

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:40.359
-Yes, right, right, right.
-"Loved the beginning."

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:42.161
-That's like every movie
I've ever done

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.596
that's based off of a book.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.197
The director's like, "So, what
did you think of the book?"

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.500
I'm like, "it's great.
It's so like the script."

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.504
[ Laughter ]
"It's so good." You know?

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.006
-You're like, "You know what?
I think once I see the movie

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:56.342
we're about to make, I'll have a
real understanding of the book."

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.411
[ Laughter ]
-We're on the same page.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:01.380
-I know you're about to go L.A.
after this.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.815
-Yes.
-You just did some London,

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:06.152
and then you get to go home,
thankfully, for the holidays.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.387
Are you looking forward to going
back, being with your family?

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:11.156
-I am. I am.
I'm very stressed, though,

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:13.092
because, you know, naturally
with a press tour,

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.994
you're very busy -- I haven't
done any Christmas shopping yet.

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.963
-Yeah.
-I don't think I can say to

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:20.032
my family that me coming back
for Christmas

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.468
is enough of a gift.
-Right.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:25.138
-But it is, right?
-Yeah, I mean, look.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.440
-Come on. Who wants me to
come over for Christmas?

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.410
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.545
-I want to say this --
no exaggeration.

00:03:33.545 --> 00:03:36.282
If you came and spent Christmas
with me, that would be enough.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.451
-Right. Vice versa.
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.252
-Are we doing this?
Are we doing this?

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:42.288
-I think we're doing this.
Honey...

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.523
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.992
Honey, tell the kids
I'm not coming home.

00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:49.762
I'm hanging out with Tom.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.931
I was wondering about
your family, 'cause I know

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.000
you're very close with
your brothers

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.635
and your family in general,
but they obviously understand

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:58.404
what you're going through
as far as how busy you are.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.772
-Right.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.407
-But they're not gonna let you
off the hook, are they?

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:02.942
-No.
-Yeah.

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:06.245
-They're really not, and I'm
gonna find myself Christmas Eve

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.046
running around like
a headless chicken,

00:04:08.046 --> 00:04:11.083
buying socks, tea towels.
-Right.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.319
-Meaningless stuff, you know?

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.187
Nice card.
I'll write a nice card.

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:17.590
"Dear Mum, merry Christmas.
Tom."

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.726
-You get a sweatshirt
that says "Heathrow."

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.995
-Yeah, exactly! Yeah.
"I love New York."

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:24.129
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.598
-"These are very rare.

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:29.669
This is the only replica Statue
of Liberty they ever made."

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.805
-It cost me a whole $9.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.474
-We also talked backstage about
that you were very lucky to do

00:04:35.474 --> 00:04:37.776
back-to-back films where
you managed to get through

00:04:37.776 --> 00:04:39.745
without any COVID shutdowns.
-Yes.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:42.648
-Which is very hard this day
and age but possible

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.484
because people take it
so seriously, right?

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:48.020
The COVID protocols
in place are massive.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.356
-I mean, it's important,
and I think, you know,

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.090
when it comes to
something like that,

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:55.961
the rules really stem
from the top, you know?

00:04:55.961 --> 00:04:58.630
Playing Spider-Man on set, you
have a responsibility to follow

00:04:58.630 --> 00:04:59.932
the rules so that everyone else

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:02.068
sees you doing it
so they copy you.

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:04.504
That said, there were times

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:05.804
that we would have a bit of fun
with it.

00:05:05.804 --> 00:05:08.774
I remember in
the Spider-Man suit,

00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:13.512
because the thing is so tight,
the zip sometimes gets stuck.

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:15.881
And it's a nightmare.
I'll have like half of it off,

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:18.451
and I'm like, "Please, just get
this thing off of me."

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:22.721
And we have a bottle of lube
that we, like, squirt on

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:25.124
the zip to, like, get it open
and stuff.

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.260
-Yeah, that's why we have one,
too, yeah.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.595
-That's why we have
bottles of lube.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.565
-Yeah, because zippers.
-Right.

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:35.401
But anyway, we were on set,
and Mitch Bell was there.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.269
Mitch Bell is one of our
big Marvel producers.

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:39.838
He's in charge of the money, so,
you know, like, a COVID shutdown

00:05:39.838 --> 00:05:41.173
for him is a very serious thing

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:42.775
and he's taking it
very seriously.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.044
And this bottle of lube
does suspiciously

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.379
look like a bottle of
hand sanitizer.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:49.949
So, he walks over and he's
chatting to me, and he's like,

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.550
"Hey, man, can I get some of
that hand sanitizer?"

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.785
And I look at my brother Harry,

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:54.954
and I'm like, "This is about to
be golden."

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.055
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.191
So, I'm squeezing all this stuff
on him.

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:00.593
I'm squeezing it, squeezing it,
squeezing it, and he walks off,

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:01.827
and you can see him on set like,

00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:04.363
"This goddamn hand sanitizer
won't go."

00:06:04.363 --> 00:06:06.165
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.200
And then the best thing --
At the end of the day,

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.669
the same thing happened with
the boom op.

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:13.005
So, he's doing a scene,
and I can see him like this.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.974
He's like,
"I can't hold on to the boom."

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.543
[ Laughter ]
"It's so slippery everywhere."

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:19.578
I promise that's the only two
times we did it, though.

00:06:19.578 --> 00:06:20.879
-That's right.

00:06:20.879 --> 00:06:24.216
The idea of you half in a
Spider-Man suit, I don't know --

00:06:24.216 --> 00:06:26.952
Have you ever gone to
the "Sesame Street" studios?

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:28.587
-I have not.
-'Cause the one thing

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:31.590
they tell you is, like, you
cannot take any photos of,

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.059
like, the muppets,
like, at rest, right,

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:35.995
'cause it would be
too terrifying for children.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:38.063
-Sitting there with a beer,
like, smoking a cigarette.

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:39.965
-Or it's just like,
you know, like that.

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:41.100
[ Laughter ]
-Right, right, right.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.601
Just a dead muppet.
-Yeah.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:45.137
I feel like the same about --
like, I would never want to see

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:48.140
a photo of, like, Spider-Man
half in and out of his suit,

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:49.609
just having given up.

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:52.110
-It's not attractive.
It's not flattering.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.280
And it also comes with
a lot of me being like,

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.115
"Get it off! Get it off!
Get it off!"

00:06:56.115 --> 00:06:58.283
I've got, like, the neck stuck
over my mouth.

00:06:58.283 --> 00:07:00.919
I'm suffocating.
Director's giving me notes.

00:07:00.919 --> 00:07:02.654
It's just -- It's a tough time.

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:05.658
-Well, the good news is
it pays off on screen.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:06.959
We're going to be right back

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:09.028
with more from Tom Holland
after this.

